  <ym-title|Proof status><label|proof-status>

  The lattice-to-continuum construction in this working draft is conditional.
  The opening section and the individual lemmas record the estimates still
  needed for the selected family of Wilson lattice measures.

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Sections B and C still require uniform bounds for the actual
    differentiated response kernels and sector determinants, and an exact
    comparison of large-field masks and the fine-field domains on which
    Taylor estimates apply.

    <item>Sections D and E give reductions for the cutoff comparison. The
    actual common domains, convergence on fixed inputs and uniform
    output-tail estimates still need proofs. The fixed-ratio coupling readout
    also depends on convergence of the incoming classical coefficients.

    <item>Section E still requires bounds for the terms created by joining
    several insertions across scales, including the restart at the stopping
    level, and the guarded joint Gaussian comparison for the physical
    insertions.

    <item>The short-distance trace coefficient in Section I additionally
    requires the quantitative transfer of the physical coefficient maps along
    the same scale history.
  </itemize-minus>

  The independently reviewed local changes include the free two-form
  transfer, the geometry used in the reflected finite-volume calculation and
  preservation of the partition and marked integrals under normalized
  comparison kernels.

  The full source archive was rebuilt in a fresh directory. The resulting PDF
  had 306 pages. The distributed PDF was checked against the source manifest.
  The review checked the local mathematical changes under their stated
  hypotheses. Review is invited on the outstanding estimates and their
  application to the construction.
